{% import 'fxc/map.jinja' as fxc_root with context %}
{#- The ceiling on OFX throughput. Four served the demo's own agents; 512 Locust investors
    offer ~340 orders/s, where four threads are a tail-latency trap (one GC pause queues
    everything). Raising it costs ~1 MB of stack each.

    Per SYMBOL, not divided across them: dividing would leave each of 25 names too thin to
    absorb 512 investors, and would silently dilute every existing name when a 26th lists.
    issue - 2*mm is the reserve opened accounts draw their shares from.

    '*' = every listed equity (InstrumentCatalog.resolveSymbols). Blank price = each
    symbol's own catalog reference price; a single scalar marked 25 issuers at one price.

    Opened investor accounts now carry stock in EVERY listed name, transferred off the
    issuer's reserve rather than minted (fxc/docs/PROBLEMS.md P24, root P19). Without it a
    rando investor rejects 24 of 25 sells and 24 books never get an ask. 20 x 25 names is
    ~$30k of stock against $100k cash, and the reserve covers 15,000 accounts. #}
